doc.add_page_break();h('Abstract')
p('TournamentVault V3 escrows the exact ETH prize at creation and an optional LRT bonus before registration opens. Fixed rules, distinct organizer/referee/resolver roles, evidence commitments, participant objections and individual withdrawals govern the tournament lifecycle. The current V3-only suite passes 51 automated tests. A six-account Sepolia wallet demonstration completed registration, referee submission, objection, arbitration, all three winner withdrawals, organizer fee withdrawal and an exchange round trip. Separate liabilities distinguish prize custody, entry fees and exchange backing. This report explains the implemented controls, recorded evidence and operational assumptions.')
h('Table of Contents');z=p();fld=OxmlElement('w:fldSimple');fld.set(qn('w:instr'),'TOC \\o "1-2" \\h \\z \\u');z._p.append(fld)
doc.add_page_break();h('1. Project Overview');h('1.1 Project Title',2);p('TournamentVault ETH Prize Escrow for Esports Tournaments')
p('V3 denotes the third version of the project, developed through two preceding rounds of revision.');h('1.2 Objectives',2);p('Make advertised prize funding observable before a player enters; enforce fixed shares and exact fees; separate result and dispute permissions; provide recoverable deadline exits; and validate balances, events and rejected operations using repeatable tests and public transactions.')
h('1.3 Background and Motivation',2);p('Players otherwise depend on an organizer to retain and distribute promised prizes after an off-chain match. A public smart contract lets entrants inspect custody and immutable terms, and lets winners withdraw credited assets. A conventional database can record scores, but cannot independently enforce custody of wallet-held ETH. Match interpretation remains a human decision outside the chain.')
h('1.4 Scope and Limitations',2);p('The system supports ETH prizes, optional LRT bonuses, exact ETH fees, ranked results, one tournament-level dispute, resolver correction, timeout cancellation, refunds and a separate fixed-rate exchange. Referee and resolver addresses are distinct but their independence and honesty are social assumptions. Evidence hashes commit to supplied records; they do not establish match truth or preserve the underlying files. LRT redemption requires available reserves. Demonstrations use test assets and simulated match evidence.')
h('2. System Design');h('2.1 Architecture Overview',2);p('The browser interface uses ethers and MetaMask. LearningRewardToken provides fixed-supply ERC20 LRT. TournamentVaultV3 escrows the main ETH prize and optional bonus, records entrants and ranked credits, and handles fees. LRTExchange holds independent token inventory and ETH backing. Wallet signatures stay in MetaMask; the page uses public addresses and ABI calls. Gameplay records remain off-chain, with hashes on-chain.')
h('2.2 User Roles and Access Control',2)
table(['Role','Permissions'],[['Organizer','Creates fixed rules, escrows ETH, opens with bonus, cancels before first entry, recovers cancelled prize, withdraws settled fees'],['Referee','Submits initial registered ranking while Locked before result deadline'],['Resolver','Confirms or replaces ranking while Disputed before resolution deadline'],['Player','Registers with exact fee, objects in time, claims refund, withdraws own prize credits'],['Any caller','Locks roster after close, finalizes unchallenged result, triggers eligible timeout cancellation']])
p('Roles are per tournament; organizer, referee and resolver must differ and cannot register in that event. msg.sender establishes authorization. The six public demo accounts are account 1 organizer, account 2 referee, account 3 resolver and accounts 4-6 players. A credit owner can choose a different nonzero receiving address.')
p('The interface keeps tournament, referee, resolver and objection controls visible. Before any wallet transaction or token approval, a click refreshes the selected event and checks the current account, state, deadlines and credits. An ineligible click shows a message and requests no transaction. Contract authorization remains the final enforcement layer.');h('2.3 Data and Process Design',2);p('Tournament stores roles, State, immutable Rules, player count, deadlines, fees, funding flag, evidence hash, winners and basis-point shares. Mappings track registrations, refund claims and individual ETH/LRT credits. Aggregate ETH and token liabilities track obligations independently of actual asset balances.')
p('Draft -> RegistrationOpen -> Locked -> ResultPending -> Finalized. Objection routes ResultPending -> Disputed -> Finalized. Organizer cancellation is available only before the first player joins. Roster locking after registration closes cancels if entrants are fewer than paid ranks. Expired drafts, abandoned results and unresolved disputes have permissionless cancellation paths. Cancellation enables individual fee refunds and organizer prize recovery. Deadlines require transactions; wall-clock expiry alone does not update state.')
h('2.4 Technology Stack',2);table(['Component','Version or configuration'],[[k,v] for k,v in json.loads((R/'package.json').read_text())['devDependencies'].items()]);p('Solidity optimizer enabled with 200 runs; Cancun EVM. The pinned local solc package avoids a separate compiler download. Node.js 22 or 24 and npm are prerequisites. Browser interaction uses MetaMask and Sepolia RPC; verification uses Etherscan. '+ack)
h('3. Smart Contract Details');h('3.1 Contract Functionality',2);p('LearningRewardToken mints the configured supply once at deployment and exposes standard ERC20 transfers/approvals. TournamentVaultV3 implements prize custody and the event lifecycle. LRTExchange sells existing inventory at 1 LRT per 1,000,000,000 wei, accepts approved tokens subject to available backing, and reserves ETH credits for a separate withdrawal. Returned tokens remain inventory; the contract has no privileged backing withdrawal.')
h('3.2 Interface Description',2)
table(['Function','Inputs and result','Main rejection'],[['createTournament','Rules, roles, shares; exact ETH prize','Invalid amount, roles, capacity, shares or deadlines'],['fundAndOpen / register','Bonus deposit / exact entry fee','Wrong role/state, missing allowance, full/duplicate/late entry'],['lockRegistration','Event ID; lock or cancel insufficient roster','Wrong state or early call'],['submitResult','ID, distinct registered winners, hash','Wrong referee/state, invalid ranking, expired result'],['raiseDispute / resolveDispute','Reason hash / corrected ranking and hash','Wrong participant/resolver/state, empty evidence, expired window'],['finalizeResult','Credits ranked prizes and organizer fees','Disputed or objection window still open'],['cancelTournament / cancelExpired','Pre-entry organizer cancellation / eligible timeout','Entrants present, terminal state, not expired'],['claimRefund / refundOrganizer','Own fee credit / return prize escrow','Not cancelled, unauthorized or repeated claim'],['withdrawPrize / withdrawETH','Own credits to chosen nonzero recipient','No credit, zero recipient, failed transfer'],['buy / redeem / withdrawETH (exchange)','Payment / approved tokens / own ETH credit','Inventory, precision, reserve, allowance or credit checks']])
h('3.3 Important Implementation Decisions',2);p('Prize ETH is escrowed immediately at creation; a bonus is transferred before accepting entrants. Entry fees remain a separate organizer entitlement only after finalization. Settlement assigns credits rather than pushing every payout, so one recipient cannot block all winners. Credits and aggregate liabilities decrease before interaction; a failed transfer rolls the transaction back. Ranked loops are bounded to 32 ranks and total entrants to 256. The last rank receives any division remainder, conserving the full prize. Evidence hashes contain no private match data.')
h('3.4 Representative Code Excerpts',2);code('require(msg.value == rules.ethPrize, "Invalid ETH prize");\nrequire(t.playerCount == 0, "Players already registered");\nrequire(msg.sender == t.referee, "Only referee");\nrequire(ethAmount > 0 || lrtAmount > 0, "No credit");\nethPrizeCredits[id][msg.sender] = 0; prizeCredits[id][msg.sender] = 0;');p('These excerpts summarize the controls; Appendix A supplies the full submitted source with its actual combined conditions. All three withdrawals that make external transfers use nonReentrant, validate recipients and check delivery success.')
h('4. Deployment on Testnet');h('4.1 Deployment Configuration',2);p('Ethereum Sepolia, chain ID 11155111. Compiler v0.8.26+commit.8a97fa7a, optimizer enabled with 200 runs, Cancun. Deployment tool: ui/deploy.html and ui/deploy-wallet.js using ethers 6.17.0 and MetaMask. The deploying account is 0xdE3d23a1245f07859279b759b528615Eb55BcAc4. No externally linked libraries are used. Times below are mined block timestamps in UTC.')
