p('Token arguments are treasury address and base-unit supply (1,000,000 LRT with 18 decimals). Vault and exchange each receive the new token address. Prize amounts, fees, roles and deadlines belong to later tournament creation, not contract constructors.')
h('4.3 Etherscan Verification',2);p('deployment/sepolia-v3-read-only-check.json records successful deployment receipts, creation input equality including constructor encoding, runtime equality excluding immutable substitutions and verified explorer source for each contract. Explorer constructor-metadata comparison is false for the token and exchange in that snapshot, while actual deployment transaction input matching is true; the transaction encoding is the authoritative submitted constructor evidence. The vault metadata comparison is true. The project does not equate that metadata field with a runtime mismatch. Direct verified-source links appear above.')
h('5. Test Cases and Validation');h('5.1 Testing Environment',2);p('The submitted suites run against Hardhat local chain 31337 using isolated fixtures, time manipulation, distinct signers, event assertions, revert checks and balance/credit assertions. The malicious PaymentReceiver fixture rejects payment or attempts a nested withdrawal. Commands: npm ci; npm run compile; npm test. The current run passes 51 tests. Public Sepolia transactions are a separate integration demonstration; local failure and boundary assertions are not claimed as failed public transactions.')
h('5.2 Test-Case Summary',2)
