h('6. Smart Contract Security Audit');h('6.1 Audit Scope and Methodology',2);p('The current scope is the three V3 production contracts and their interaction with the pinned token, receiver fixture and wallet interface. npm run analyze compiles an AST with a small explicit rule set and records source hashes, bytecode sizes and diagnostics. It is combined with manual review and adversarial unit tests. The current AST scan has 2,081 project nodes, zero compiler errors and 21 review prompts; these prompts are review items, not confirmed vulnerability severities. The full raw output is audit/static-analysis.json. No claim of a complete security audit or formal verification is made.')
h('6.2 Findings Summary',2)
table(['ID and scope','Impact and severity','Control and retest status'],[['S01 roles and msg.sender','Unauthorized result or credit claims; application risk High','Role checks and owner-scoped credits; non-referee, non-resolver and outsider tests pass'],['S02 external calls','Reentry, duplicate payout or lost credit; application risk High','Effects before interactions, nonReentrant, checked calls; rejected delivery/reentry and repeat withdrawal tests pass'],['S03 timestamp rules','Early/late operations and unresolved states; Review / residual Low','Consistent gates and timeout exits; exact registration/result/dispute/resolution boundaries pass'],['S04 bounded loops','Gas exhaustion with large rankings; Review','Max 32 ranks and 256 entrants, no all-player refund loop. Capacity rejection passes; maximum-rank gas benchmarking remains future work'],['S05 separate liabilities','Prize or reserve insolvency; application risk High','Exact escrow, individual obligations, reserve check; full payout conservation and insufficient-reserve tests pass'],['S06 off-chain governance','Dishonest or unavailable evidence; residual governance risk','Distinct referee/resolver, participant objection and hashes; correction/timeout tests pass, human judgment remains trusted']])
h('6.3 Manual Security Review',2);p('SafeERC20 handles token return semantics. Solidity 0.8 checked arithmetic is used; Math.mulDiv computes ranked fractions and the final rank receives remainder. Immutable token bindings restrict supported assets to the submitted standard fixed-supply LRT. Nonzero recipients and credit ownership prevent unauthorized withdrawals. Refunding each player separately avoids a recipient blocking other participants. Timestamp precision does not guarantee transaction inclusion, so operators must use practical margins. The contracts have no administrator reserve sweep, emergency pause or upgrade path. Synthetic public demonstration data avoids personal information; no private keys, seed phrases or credentials are part of the repository.')
h('7. Conclusion and Future Work');h('7.1 Conclusion',2);p('The project implements funded ETH prize custody, optional LRT bonuses, exact entry fees, fixed ranked shares, separate result/arbitration permissions, objections, deadline recovery and individual withdrawals. The current 51-test suite validates local positive, negative and boundary behavior, while the public wallet demonstration supplies independent receipts for the complete contested settlement and exchange workflow. The design lesson is to separate asset custody, entitlements and liquidity across the contracts.')
h('7.2 Future Work',2);p('Potential extensions include independently governed arbitration, signed structured evidence with availability commitments, reserve monitoring and property-based state-machine testing. Maximum-rank gas benchmarking and additional adversarial recipient cases could extend the current verification scope. These improvements preserve the clear custody and permission model.')
h('References');p('OpenZeppelin Contracts 5.x documentation: https://docs.openzeppelin.com/contracts/5.x/');p('Hardhat documentation: https://v2.hardhat.org/');p('Solidity security considerations: https://docs.soliditylang.org/en/v0.8.26/security-considerations.html');p('ethers v6 documentation: https://docs.ethers.org/v6/');p('CSIT5760 supplied project guideline and final report template, Academic Year 2026-2027.');p(ack)
